{#-
  OpenVDM cruise README template (Jinja2, https://jinja.palletsprojects.com/).

  The installer copies this file to server/etc/cruise_readme.md.j2 when
  that doesn't exist yet; edit the copy (or set cruiseReadme.template in
  openvdm.yaml) to change the README. OpenVDM doesn't use this .dist file
  itself: without the copy, the README isn't written. The variables are
  described in build_cruise_readme_context() in server/lib/readme.py. The
  README is rebuilt whenever the cruise config is exported: Setup New
  Cruise, Edit Cruise, Finalize Cruise and Export OpenVDM Config.
-#}
# Cruise {{ cruise.cruiseID }}{% if cruise.cruiseName %}: {{ cruise.cruiseName }}{% endif %}


{% if cruise.cruiseDescription %}
{{ cruise.cruiseDescription }}

{% endif %}
This directory holds the data collected during cruise {{ cruise.cruiseID }}{% if vessel.name %} aboard {{ vessel.name }}{% endif %}, organized by OpenVDM (Open Vessel Data Management).

## Cruise

{% if vessel.name %}
- **Vessel:** {{ vessel.name }}{% if vessel.r2r and vessel.r2r.vesselID %} (R2R vessel ID {{ vessel.r2r.vesselID }}){% endif %}

{% endif %}
{% if cruise.cruisePI %}
- **Chief scientist:** {{ cruise.cruisePI }}
{% endif %}
{% if cruise.cruiseStartDate or cruise.cruiseEndDate %}
- **Dates:** {{ cruise.cruiseStartDate or "?" }} to {{ cruise.cruiseEndDate or "?" }}
{% endif %}
{% if cruise.cruiseStartPort or cruise.cruiseEndPort %}
- **Ports:** {{ cruise.cruiseStartPort or "?" }} to {{ cruise.cruiseEndPort or "?" }}
{% endif %}
{% if cruise.cruiseLocation %}
- **Location:** {{ cruise.cruiseLocation }}
{% endif %}
{% if cruise.cruiseExtent %}
- **Extent:** {{ cruise.cruiseExtent.westernmost }} to {{ cruise.cruiseExtent.easternmost }} longitude, {{ cruise.cruiseExtent.southernmost }} to {{ cruise.cruiseExtent.northernmost }} latitude (decimal degrees)
{% endif %}
{% if vessel.contact and (vessel.contact.institution or vessel.contact.email) %}
- **Contact:** {{ [vessel.contact.institution, vessel.contact.email] | select | join(", ") }}
{% endif %}

## Directory layout
Paths are relative to this directory.
{# A description is Markdown that goes under its folder's heading: a
   paragraph, a **Files:** list and an optional **Sub-directories:** list
   (#499). Each line ends in two spaces, a Markdown line break, so a single
   line break stays one, as on OpenVDM's pages (#460) #}

{% macro entry(d) %}
#### `{{ d.destDir }}{{ "" if d.file else "/" }}`: {{ d.longName or d.name }}
{% if d.description %}

{{ d.description | replace("\r\n", "\n") | replace("\n", "  \n") }}

{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
{% set entries = [
    {"destDir": files.readme, "longName": "this file", "file": true},
    {"destDir": files.cruise_config, "longName": "the cruise's OpenVDM configuration (JSON): the cruise details above and the directory layout", "file": true},
    {"destDir": files.md5_summary, "longName": "the MD5 checksum of every file in this directory, to check that a copy of it is complete and unchanged", "file": true},
    {"destDir": files.md5_summary_md5, "longName": "the MD5 checksum of `" ~ files.md5_summary ~ "` itself", "file": true},
] + collection_systems + extra_directories %}
{% if files.data_dashboard_manifest %}
{% set entries = entries + [
    {"destDir": files.data_dashboard_manifest, "longName": "the list of the files behind OpenVDM's Data Dashboard: the data and quality test results extracted from the raw files", "file": true},
] %}
{% endif %}
{% if lowerings %}
{% set entries = entries + [{
    "destDir": lowerings.base_dir,
    "longName": "Lowerings",
    "description": "A directory for each lowering (vehicle dive or deployment), named by its lowering ID: `" ~ lowerings.base_dir ~ "/<loweringID>/`."
}] %}
{% endif %}
{% for d in entries | sort(attribute="destDir") %}
{{ entry(d) }}
{%- endfor %}

---

Generated by OpenVDM{% if openvdm_version %} {{ openvdm_version }}{% endif %} on {{ generated_on }}.
